# AI working state

Globally-useful state only. Detail lives in `state/<track>.md` — see the
index below. Read this file first every session; read a track's state file
only when you are touching that track.

## Latest

The walking skeleton is up: config, wire codecs, extension points, and a
single-channel WebSocket chat server with private messages, all tested
against real clients over an `httptest.Server`. Three goroutines per
connection (read pump, broadcast write pump, private pump); the wire
format is negotiated by subprotocol with MessagePack and JSON behind one
`Codec` interface; authentication, chatter data, moderation and
persistence are interfaces in `internal/hook` that the core never imports
an implementation of. Detail in `state/server.md`; the fan-out underneath
it is in `state/broadcast.md`. Next: channels — `JOIN`/`PART`/`NAMES` and
a lookup from channel name to its own set of per-codec rings.

## State file index

- `state/broadcast.md` — `internal/broadcast`, the fan-out primitive and
  its comparative benchmark harness.
- `state/server.md` — config, wire codecs, extension points, and the
  connection handling built on the fan-out.

